    "commit_message": "Health OSINT: close the Chronic Pain coverage gap (source #27)\n\nCaptain: work the Chronic Pain gap flagged in the priority-domains work.\nReused Europe PMC \u2014 the same real, already-proven source the 4\nneurodivergence sources use (migration 0160) \u2014 rather than integrating a\nnew vendor: same endpoint shape, only the query and domain classifier\ndiffer. Confirmed live before writing anything: field-restricted\nTITLE:/ABSTRACT: query for chronic pain/fibromyalgia/central\nsensitization/neuropathic pain returns 110,091 hits, current 2026\nresults, overwhelmingly on-topic.\n\nNew tools/health-osint/parsers/parse_europepmc_chronic_pain.py (mirrors\nparse_europepmc_neurodivergence.py's structure exactly) with 8\nchronic_pain_* sub-tags (general, lived_experience, central_sensitization,\nfibromyalgia, neuropathic, medication, treatment, flare), same\nmost-specific-first keyword classification as the neuro_* tags. Migration\n0178 registers the source + fetch config, additive only.\n\nRan real ingestion end-to-end (not just a dry parser test): 25/25 signals\nfetched and inserted live, classified across 5 of the 8 sub-tags with\nreal, sensible distribution (chronic_pain 12, chronic_pain_neuropathic 6,\nchronic_pain_medication 3, chronic_pain_central_sensitization 3,\nchronic_pain_fibromyalgia 1).\n\nAdded all 8 chronic_pain_* tags to PRIORITY_DOMAINS in both\npriority_domains.py and its TypeScript mirror\n(intelligence-summary/route.ts) \u2014 Chronic Pain now gets the same\nlower-evidence-bar curation treatment and display priority as the other\n6 named areas.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011Q88CdbAYk33hiVJ7zUWs8",
